s"}],"commentType":"FUNCTION"},{"commentType":"CATALYTIC ACTIVITY","reaction":{"name":"UTP + L-glutamine + ATP + H2O = CTP + L-glutamate + ADP + phosphate + 2 H(+)","reactionCrossReferences":[{"database":"Rhea","id":"RHEA:26426"},{"database":"ChEBI","id":"CHEBI:15377"},{"database":"ChEBI","id":"CHEBI:15378"},{"database":"ChEBI","id":"CHEBI:29985"},{"database":"ChEBI","id":"CHEBI:30616"},{"database":"ChEBI","id":"CHEBI:37563"},{"database":"ChEBI","id":"CHEBI:43474"},{"database":"ChEBI","id":"CHEBI:46398"},{"database":"ChEBI","id":"CHEBI:58359"},{"database":"ChEBI","id":"CHEBI:456216"}],"ecNumber":"6.3.4.2","evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000255","source":"HAMAP-Rule","id":"MF_01227"}]}},{"commentType":"CATALYTIC ACTIVITY","reaction":{"name":"L-glutamine + H2O = L-glutamate + NH4(+)","reactionCrossReferences":[{"database":"Rhea","id":"RHEA:15889"},{"database":"ChEBI","id":"CHEBI:15377"},{"database":"ChEBI","id":"CHEBI:28938"},{"database":"ChEBI","id":"CHEBI:29985"},{"database":"ChEBI","id":"CHEBI:58359"}],"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000255","source":"HAMAP-Rule","id":"MF_01227"}]}},{"commentType":"CATALYTIC ACTIVITY","reaction":{"name":"UTP + NH4(+) + ATP = CTP + ADP + phosphate + 2 H(+)","reactionCrossReferences":[{"database":"Rhea","id":"RHEA:16597"},{"database":"ChEBI","id":"CHEBI:15378"},{"database":"ChEBI","id":"CHEBI:28938"},{"database":"ChEBI","id":"CHEBI:30616"},{"database":"ChEBI","id":"CHEBI:37563"},{"database":"ChEBI","id":"CHEBI:43474"},{"database":"ChEBI","id":"CHEBI:46398"},{"database":"ChEBI","id":"CHEBI:456216"}],"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000255","source":"HAMAP-Rule","id":"MF_01227"}]}},{"texts":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000255","source":"HAMAP-Rule","id":"MF_01227"}],"value":"Allosterically activated by GTP, when glutamine is the substrate; GTP has no effect on the reaction when ammonia is the substrate. The allosteric effector GTP functions by stabilizing the protein conformation that binds the tetrahedral intermediate(s) formed during glutamine hydrolysis. Inhibited by the product CTP, via allosteric rather than competitive inhibition"}],"commentType":"ACTIVITY REGULATION"},{"texts":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000255","source":"HAMAP-Rule","id":"MF_01227"}],"value":"Pyrimidine metabolism; CTP biosynthesis via de novo pathway; CTP from UDP: step 2/2"}],"commentType":"PATHWAY"},{"texts":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000255","source":"HAMAP-Rule","id":"MF_01227"}],"value":"Homotetramer"}],"commentType":"SUBUNIT"},{"texts":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000255","source":"HAMAP-Rule","id":"MF_01227"}],"value":"CTPSs have evolved a hybrid strategy for distinguishing between UTP and CTP. The overlapping regions of the product feedback inhibitory and substrate sites recognize a common feature in both compounds, the triphosphate moiety. To differentiate isosteric substrate and product pyrimidine rings, an additional pocket far from the expected kinase/ligase catalytic site, specifically recognizes the cytosine and ribose portions of the product inhibitor"}],"commentType":"MISCELLANEOUS"},{"texts":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000255","source":"HAMAP-Rule","id":"MF_01227"}],"value":"Belongs to the CTP synthase family"}],"commentType":"SIMILARITY"}],"features":[{"type":"Chain","location":{"start":{"value":1,"modifier":"EXACT"},"end":{"value":545,"modifier":"EXACT"}},"description":"CTP synthase","featureId":"PRO_1000139368"},{"type":"Domain","location":{"start":{"value":291,"modifier":"EXACT"},"end":{"value":542,"modifier":"EXACT"}},"description":"Glutamine amidotransferase type-1","evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000255","source":"HAMAP-Rule","id":"MF_01227"}]},{"type":"Region","location":{"start":{"value":1,"modifier":"EXACT"},"end":{"value":266,"modifier":"EXACT"}},"description":"Amidoligase domain","evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000255","source":"HAMAP-Rule","id":"MF_01227"}]},{"type":"Active site","location":{"start":{"value":379,"modifier":"EXACT"},"e